# yamls/us/reloc_*.yml are now COMMITTED. They're regenerated from
# tools/reloc_data_symbols.us.txt + ROM by tools/generate_yamls.py;
# regen and re-commit when reloc_data_symbols.us.txt changes (rare for
# a frozen v1.0). Same pattern as port/resource/RelocFileTable.cpp.
# Their content (file_id ↔ symbol ↔ ROM offset/size) is a strict
# subset of upstream ssb-decomp-re's smashbrothers.us.yaml splat
# config — standard decomp metadata, no ROM bytes.

# Decomp artifacts
asm/
*.d
*.ld
*.o
*.credits.encoded
*.credits.metadata
assets/*
!assets/icon.png
!assets/icon.ico
!assets/icon-jp.png
!assets/icon-jp.ico
!assets/SmashBrotatoes.svg
!assets/readme-stats/
!assets/readme-stats/*.svg
!assets/custom/
!assets/custom/fonts/
!assets/custom/fonts/*
__pycache__
bin/
# Hi-res texture pack drops — port/hires/HiResPack scans CWD-relative
# `mods/` on Linux dev launches before falling back to <app-data>/mods/,
# so it's common to end up with a pack folder at the repo root during
# pack-authoring sessions. Always user-private content, never tracked.
# Root-anchored: an unanchored `mods/` also matched port/mods/ (the hook
# system source) and workspace/*/mods/, silently dropping new files there.
/mods/
relocAssets/
undefined*
ctx.c
ctx.c.m2c
m2cfiles/
us_report.json

# Decomp tools (not needed for port)
tools/ido-recomp/
tools/vpk0cmd
tools/halAssetTool

# The generated reloc artifacts are COMMITTED (not ignored) so CI and fresh
# clones build without the ROM or the Python generators:
#   include/reloc_data.{us,jp}.h, port/resource/RelocFileTable.{us,jp}.cpp,
#   yamls/us/reloc_*.yml — regenerated from tools/reloc_data_symbols.{us,jp}.txt
#   (via the GenerateRelocArtifacts / RegenerateRelocYamls CMake targets) and
#   re-committed when that source changes. The rule below only ignores a
#   legacy symbols/ copy of the source, if one is ever produced.
symbols/reloc_data_symbols.*

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
imgui.ini

# vcpkg (bootstrapped at build time)
_packages/
vcpkg_installed/

